 "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18775, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SHpovjEN8Texbr749nmtZ2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18775, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LmtDXDd1vrL43QnLbzg9eG", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19075, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LmtDXDd1vrL43QnLbzg9eG", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19075, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LmtDXDd1vrL43QnLbzg9eG", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23645, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01FxtXXcfXXi6W96Kn1qZy7N", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway (orchestrator error) after updating us-east only. A retry completed the rollout to us-west and eu-west. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator rollout error, and work out why a release that was unhealthy in staging was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54245, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FxtXXcfXXi6W96Kn1qZy7N", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54245, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FxtXXcfXXi6W96Kn1qZy7N", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55324, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LxfBeU1QojTCK5UryMgJbF", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55624, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LxfBeU1QojTCK5UryMgJbF", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55624, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LxfBeU1QojTCK5UryMgJbF", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60795, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy, and the SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release is v2.3.1. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging. The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0, so I rolled back to that.\n- The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error. It updated us-east only, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a fixed version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again, and it finished.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west now all run v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created: **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api, open). I didn't resend it, so there's only one incident and only one page went out.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and three follow-ups:\n  - Find what caused v2.3.1 to fail.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n  - Work out how a release that failed in staging got deployed to production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0113FqAxqFbMHtnrkCY3uNQE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UHsRB2oD2MvSDxn4aP6UMU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018pCyTmUkGagTvhSLRq4F5Q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YYzsHP6xWTpvQy4MTokV7Q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Partial rollback: us-east is now on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Since a rollback to a set version is safe to repeat, I'm retrying it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017Y4CJ97oVJS3og9p4CYYYG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SHpovjEN8Texbr749nmtZ2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LmtDXDd1vrL43QnLbzg9eG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FxtXXcfXXi6W96Kn1qZy7N", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway (orchestrator error) after updating us-east only. A retry completed the rollout to us-west and eu-west. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator rollout error, and work out why a release that was unhealthy in staging was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LxfBeU1QojTCK5UryMgJbF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy, and the SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release is v2.3.1. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging. The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0, so I rolled back to that.\n- The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error. It updated us-east only, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a fixed version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again, and it finished.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west now all run v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created: **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api, open). I didn't resend it, so there's only one incident and only one page went out.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and three follow-ups:\n  - Find what caused v2.3.1 to fail.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n  - Work out how a release that failed in staging got deployed to production.", "type": "text"}]}]}